<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taejo of Goryeo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">877–943</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Wang Geon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taejo of Goryeo, born Wang Geon, was the founder of the Goryeo dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. A general of Taebong from a trading family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaesong">Songak</a>, he was raised to the throne in 918 after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gung-ye">Gung Ye</a>. He accepted the surrender of Silla in 935 and defeated Later Baekje in 936, reuniting the Korean peninsula.</p></div>
